#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# prime_omega

#% text
# `prime_omega(n)` gives the number of prime factors of `n` counted with multiplicity.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `prime_omega(1)` is 0; `prime_omega(p^k)` is `k`.

#% item
# `prime_omega` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
prime_omega(12)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
prime_omega(30)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
prime_omega(64)
#% output
#= 6

#% cell
prime_omega(range(10))
#% output
#= [0, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 3, 2, 2]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The sum of the exponents of the factorisation:

#% cell
[prime_omega(720), sum(factor_integer(720)[all, 2])]
#% output
#= [7, 7]

#% text
# `liouville_lambda` is `(-1)^prime_omega(n)`:

#% cell
[liouville_lambda(720), (-1)^prime_omega(720)]
#% output
#= [-1, -1]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `prime_nu`, `liouville_lambda`, `factor_integer`
